# Build
build/
.gradle/
out/
*.class
*.jar
*.war

# …EXCEPT the Gradle wrapper jar, which is an INPUT and not a build output.
#
# `*.jar` above sits under "# Build" beside build/, .gradle/, out/, *.class and
# *.war — every one of those is something the build PRODUCES. It was written to
# keep build output out of the repo, and it swallowed the one jar the build
# needs to exist before it can run.
#
# The cost was not theoretical. gradlew, gradlew.bat and
# gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties were all committed in the initial
# commit, so a clean checkout receives three files that promise a working
# wrapper and then throws
#     Error: Could not find or load main class org.gradle.wrapper.GradleWrapperMain
# on every invocation. A fresh worktree could not run ./gradlew at all, which
# means A CLEAN CHECKOUT OF THIS REPO COULD NOT RUN ITS OWN TESTS: every
# "reproduced at pristine HEAD" claim depended on somebody noticing and hand-
# copying the jar in from another checkout. The jar had never been committed on
# any ref, and no README or runbook told anyone to regenerate it.
#
# Committing the wrapper jar is the documented Gradle recommendation for
# exactly this reason. Guarded by BuildIsRunnableFromAFreshCloneSpec, which
# fails if the jar stops being tracked or its bytes change unrecorded.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Runtime data
data/
*.db
*.mv.db
*.trace.db
logs/

# Local dev artefacts that should never be committed. boot.log is the
# nohup target for bootRun; gradle.properties holds machine-local Gradle
# JVM tuning; *.output / .tmp_* are leftover agent/test artefacts. Each
# was actively dirtying `git status` and risked being accidentally
# included in a bulk `git add .`.
boot.log
gradle.properties
*.output
.tmp_*

# Scratch/working files use a leading-underscore convention: _ship_*.py
# helper scripts, _qa_boss/ prompts, _runlog*.txt logs, _append_*.css
# snippets, _jarup/ extracted jars, _screens/ captures. ~296 had been
# committed into the repo root; removed in one sweep and ignored here at
# root level so they never creep back via a bulk `git add .`.
/_*

# Editor / patch backups (e.g. WatchlistAlertService.groovy.orig)
*.orig

# Environment / secrets — only the *.example is tracked, never the real env
.env
*.env
.env.*
deploy/skinbox.env

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Node (if ever added)
node_modules/

# Docker
docker-compose.override.yml

# Claude memory (project-local, not committed)
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
**/.playwright-mcp/
cycle*.png
*.png
cloudflared.log
cloudflared/

# Python bytecode from market-research scratch scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
